      "title": "Is Taiwanese Society Prepared for a China Contingency?",
      "summary": "<p>In 2025, Michael Hunzeker and Yuster Yu wrote, &#8220;Taiwan&#8217;s Biggest Problem in Steeling Itself for War With China is Cultural,&#8221; where they argued major cultural changes were needed in both Taiwan&#8217;s military and civilian society if it were to be competitive in a conflict with China. A year later, we asked them to revisit their arguments.Image: Taiwan Presidential Office via Wikimedia CommonsIn your 2025 article, you argued that major cultural changes must take place in both the officer corps of Taiwan&#8217;s armed forces and broader society if Taiwan is to be competitive in a contingency with China. A year later,</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://warontherocks.com/is-taiwanese-society-prepared-for-a-china-contingency/\">Is Taiwanese Society Prepared for a China Contingency?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://warontherocks.com\">War on the Rocks</a>.</p>",
